{
  "title": "27: al-Naml النمل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰسٓ‌ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْقُرْاٰنِ وَكِتَابٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(1)\nTAA SIN! TILKA AAYAATUL QURAANE WA KETAABIM MOBEEN\nTa Seen These are the verses of the Qur’an, and the Book maketh the truth manifesting,\nهُدًى وَّبُشْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(2)\nHODANW WA BUSHRAA LIL-MOMENEENAL\nA guidance and glad tidings unto the believers,\nالَّذِيْنَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَ هُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(3)\nLAZEENA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM YOOQENOON\nWho establish prayer and give the poor-rate, and of the hereafter, they are sure.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ زَيَّنَّا لَهُمْ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَهُمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَؕ‏(4)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-AAKHERATE ZAYYANNAA LAHUM A-A’MAALAHUM FAHUM YA’MAHOON\nVerily, those who believe not in the hereafter, We have made their deeds fair-seeming unto them, so they wander bewildered.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَهُمْ سُوْٓءُ الْعَذَابِ وَهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ هُمُ الْاَخْسَرُوْنَ‏(5)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA LAHUM SOOO-UL A’ZAABE WA HUM FIL AAKHERATE HOMUL AKHSAROON\nThese are those for whom shall be a grievous chastisement, and (these are) they in the hereafter, who shall be the greatest losers,\nوَاِنَّكَ لَتُلَقَّى الْقُرْاٰنَ مِنْ لَّدُنْ حَكِيْمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(6)\nWA INNAKA LATOLAQQAL QURAANA MIL LADUN HAKEEMIN A’LEEM\nVerily thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) receivest the Qur’an from unto the All-Wise, All-Knowing.\nاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَهْلِهٖۤ اِنِّىْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًاؕ سَاٰتِيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ اَوْ اٰتِيْكُمْ بِشِهَابٍ قَبَسٍ لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُوْنَ‏(7)\nIZ QAALA MOOSAA LE-AHLIHI INNEE AANASTO NAARAN, SA-AATEEKUM MINHAA BEKHABARIN AW AATEEKUM BESHEHAABIN QABASIL LA-A’LLAKUM TASTALOON\nWhen said Moses unto his family, “Verily I perceive fire; soon will I bring unto you of it some tiding or bring I unto you a brand lighted, that ye may warm yourselves.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهَا نُوْدِىَ اَنْۢ بُوْرِكَ مَنْ فِى النَّارِ وَ مَنْ حَوْلَهَا ؕ وَسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(8)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHAA NOODEYA AM BOOREKA MAN FIN NAARE WA MAN HAWLAHAA, WA SUBHAANAL LAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN\nSo when he came unto it, he was called unto saying, “Blessed is whosoever is in the fire and whosoever is about it; and hallowed is God, the Lord of the worlds!\nيٰمُوْسٰۤى اِنَّهٗۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُۙ‏(9)\nYAA MOOSAA INNAHU ANAL LAAHUL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEMO\nO’ Moses! Verily it is, I am God the All-Mighty, the All-Wise,\nوَاَ لْقِ عَصَاكَ‌ ؕ فَلَمَّا رَاٰهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَاَنَّهَا جَآنٌّ وَّلّٰى مُدْبِرًا وَّلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ‌ ؕ يٰمُوْسٰى لَا تَخَفْ اِنِّىْ لَا يَخَافُ لَدَىَّ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ ‌ۖ‏(10)\nWA ALQE A’SAAKA, FALAMMAA RA-AAHAA TAHTAZZO KA-ANNAHAA JAAANNUW WALLAA MUDBERAWN WA LAM YO-A’QQIB, YAA MOOSAA LAA TAKHAF, INNEE LAA YAKHAAFO LADAYYAL MURSALOON.\nAnd cast thou down thy staff! “So when he saw it moving as if (it was) a serpent, he turned back retreating and returned not: (then it was said unto him): “O’ Moses’ Fear not! for shall not fear (My) apostles in My presence.\nاِلَّا مَنْ ظَلَمَ ثُمَّ بَدَّلَ حُسْنًۢا بَعْدَ سُوْٓءٍ فَاِنِّىْ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(11)\nILLAA MAN ZALAMA SUMMA BADDALA HUSNAM BA’DA SOOO-IN FA-INNEE GHAFOORUR RAHEEMUN\nSave he who hath been unjust, then in its place he doeth good after the evil, for verily I am the Oft-Forgiving, the All- Merciful.\nوَاَدْخِلْ يَدَكَ فِىْ جَيْبِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَآءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوْٓءٍ‌ فِىْ تِسْعِ اٰيٰتٍ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَقَوْمِهٖؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(12)\nWA ADKHIL YADAKA FEE JAYBEKA TAKHRUJ BAYZAAA-A MIN GHAIRE SOOO-IN, FEE TIS-E’ AAYAATIN ELAA FIRA’WNA WA QAWMEHI, INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nNow put thy hand into thy bosom, it shall come forth white, shining, without evil: (this is) along with the nine signs (thou wilt take) unto Pharaoh and his people; Verily, they are a transgressing people\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتْهُمْ اٰيٰتُنَا مُبْصِرَةً قَالُوْا هٰذَا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(13)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM AAYAATONAA MUBSERATAN QAALOO HAAZAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nSo when came unto them Our clear signs, said they: “this is plain sorcery.\nوَجَحَدُوْا بِهَا وَاسْتَيْقَنَتْهَاۤ اَنْفُسُهُمْ ظُلْمًا وَّعُلُوًّا‌ ؕ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(14)\nWA JAHADOO BEHAA WASTAYQANATHAA ANFOSOHUM ZULMAWN WA O’LUWWAA, FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUFSEDEEN.\nThey denied them in iniquity and arrogance while their hearts were convinced; See then how was the end of the mischief makers.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ وَ سُلَيْمٰنَ عِلْمًا‌ ۚ وَقَالَا الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ فَضَّلَنَا عَلٰى كَثِيْرٍ مِّنْ عِبَادِهِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(15)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA DAAWOODA WA SOLAYMAANA I’LMAN, WA QAALAL HAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE FAZZALANAA A’LAA KASEERIM MIN E’BAADEHIL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd indeed gave We knowledge to David and Solomon, and (both the apostles) said: “All praise is God’s, Who hath made us to excel many of the believing servants,\nوَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمٰنُ دَاوٗدَ‌ وَقَالَ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ عُلِّمْنَا مَنْطِقَ الطَّيْرِ وَاُوْتِيْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍؕ‌ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْفَضْلُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(16)\nWA WARESA SULAYMAANO DAAWOODA WA QAALA YAA AYYOHAN NAASO U’LLIMNAA MANTEQAT TAYRE WA OOTEENAA MIN KULLE SHAYIN, INNA HAAZAA LAHOWAL FAZLUL MOBEEN\nAnd Solomon inherited David, and he said “O’ people! We have been taught the language of the birds, and We have been granted (plenty) of every thing; Verily this is a manifest grace.\nوَحُشِرَ لِسُلَيْمٰنَ جُنُوْدُهٗ مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ وَالطَّيْرِ فَهُمْ يُوْزَعُوْنَ‏(17)\nWA HOSHERA LESOLAYMAANA JONOODOHU MENAL JINNE WAL INSE WAT-TAYRE FAHUM YOOZA-O’ON\nAnd gathered together unto Solomon his hosts of jinn and men and birds, then they were arrayed in ranks.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَاۤ اَتَوْا عَلٰى وَادِ النَّمْلِۙ قَالَتْ نَمْلَةٌ يّٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّمْلُ ادْخُلُوْا مَسٰكِنَكُمْ‌ۚ لَا يَحْطِمَنَّكُمْ سُلَيْمٰنُ وَجُنُوْدُهٗۙ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(18)\nHAATAA EZAA ATAW A’LAA WAADIN NAMLE, QAALAT NAMLATUYN YAA AYYOHAN NAMLUD KHOLOO MASAAKENAKUM, LAA YAHTEMANNAKUM SOLAYMAANO WA JONOODOHU, WA HUM LAA YASHO’ROON.\nUntil they came to the valley of the Ants, said an Ant (addressing the other ants of the valley): “O’ ye ants! enter ye into your dwellings, so that Solomon and his hosts may not crush ye (all) while they know it not.\nفَتَبَسَّمَ ضَاحِكًا مِّنْ قَوْلِهَا وَقَالَ رَبِّ اَوْزِعْنِىْۤ اَنْ اَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ الَّتِىْۤ اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ وَعَلٰى وَالِدَىَّ وَاَنْ اَعْمَلَ صَالِحًا تَرْضٰٮهُ وَاَدْخِلْنِىْ بِرَحْمَتِكَ فِىْ عِبَادِكَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(19)\nFATABASSAMA ZAAHEKAM MIN QAWLEHAA WA QAALA RABBE AWZE’NEE AN ASHKORA NE’MATAKAL LATEE ANA’MTA A’LAYYA WA A’LAA WAALEDAYYA WA AN A-A’MALA SAALEHAN TARZAAHO WA ADKHILNEE BERAHMATEKA FEE E’BAADEKAS SAALEHEEN.\nThen smiled (Solomon) laughing at her word, and said: “O’ My Lord! arouse me to be thankful for thy bounty which thou hast bestowed on me and my parents, and that I do good such as Thou wouldst be pleased with, and admit me by Thy mercy, among Thy righteous servants.\nوَتَفَقَّدَ الطَّيْرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِىَ لَاۤ اَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ ‌ۖ  اَمْ كَانَ مِنَ الْغَآئِبِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA TAFAQQADAT TAYRA FAQAALA MAA LEYA LAA ARAL HUDHODA, AM KAANA MENAL GHAAEBEEN.\nAnd reviewed the birds, then said: “How is it, I see not Hud-hud (Hoopoe) or is that he is among the absentees?\nلَاُعَذِّبَنَّهٗ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا اَوْ لَا۟اَذْبَحَنَّهٗۤ اَوْ لَيَاْتِيَنِّىْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(21)\nLA-O-A’ZZEBANNAHU A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAN AWLAA AZBAHANNAHU AWLAYAATEYANNEE BESULTANIM MOBEEN.\nCertainly will I chastise him with a severe chastisement, or will I certainly slaughter him, or he shall bring unto me a warrant clear,\nفَمَكَثَ غَيْرَ بَعِيْدٍ فَقَالَ اَحَطْتُّ بِمَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهٖ وَ جِئْتُكَ مِنْ سَبَاٍۢ بِنَبَاٍ يَّقِيْنٍ‏(22)\nFAMAKASA GHAYRO BA-E’EDIN FAQAALA AHATTO BEMAA LAM TOHIT BEHI WA JE’TOKA MIN SABA-IM BENABAIYN YAQEEN\nAnd he tarried not long, then (he came up in the air and) said: “I comprehend what thou comprehendeth not, and I have brought unto thee from Sheba tidings sure.\nاِنِّىْ وَجَدتُّ امْرَاَةً تَمْلِكُهُمْ وَاُوْتِيَتْ مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(23)\nINNEE WAJADTUM RA-ATAN TAMLEKOHUM WA OOTEYAT MIN KULLE SHAY-IWN WA LAHAA A’RSHUN A’ZEEM.\nVerily found I a woman ruling over them, and she hath been given plenty of every thing, and she hath a throne magnificent.\nوَجَدْتُّهَا وَقَوْمَهَا يَسْجُدُوْنَ لِلشَّمْسِ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ فَهُمْ لَا يَهْتَدُوْنَۙ‏(24)\nWA JADTOHAA WA QAWMAHAA YASJODOONA LISH-SHAMSE MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA ZAYYANA LAHOMUSH SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM FASADDATHUM A’NIS SABEELE FAHUM LAA YAHTADOON.\nAnd I found her and her people prostrating (in obeisance) unto the sun, besides God, and unto them Satan hath made their deeds fair-seeming, and thus hath turned them from the (right) way, so they are not guided aright.\nاَلَّا يَسْجُدُوْا لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ يُخْرِجُ الْخَبْءَ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُخْفُوْنَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(25)\nALLAAYASJODOO LILLAAHIL LAAZEE YUKHREJUL KHAB-A FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZE WA YA’LAMO MA TUKHFOONA WA MAA TO’LENOON.\nThat (why) they make not obeisance unto God. Who bringeth forth to light what is hid den in the heavens and the earth and what ye hide and what ye manifest,\nاَللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ ۩‏(26)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL A’ZEEM\nGod! There is no God but He! He is the Lord of ‘Arsh’, the Mighty (Throne of Supreme Authority)\nقَالَ سَنَنْظُرُ اَصَدَقْتَ اَمْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(27)\nQAALA SANANZORO A-SADAQTA AM KUNTA MENAL KAAZEBEEN\nSaid (Solomon): “We will see if thou hast uttered the truth or thou art of the liars\nاِذْهَبْ بِّكِتٰبِىْ هٰذَا فَاَلْقِهْ اِلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(28)\nIZHAB BEKETAABEE HAAZAA FA-ALQEH ELAYHIM SUMMA TAWALLA A’NHUM FANZUR MAA ZAA YARJE-O’ON\nGo thou with this letter of mine and convey it unto them, and turn away from them and see what (answer) they return\nقَالَتْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَؤُا اِنِّىْۤ اُلْقِىَ اِلَىَّ كِتٰبٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(29)\nQAALAT YAA-AYYOHAL MALA-O INNEE ULQEYA ELAYYA KETAABUN KAREEM.\nSaid (the Queen of Sheba) “O’ ye Chiefs! Verily, has been delivered unto me a letter honourable!\nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ سُلَيْمٰنَ وَاِنَّهٗ بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِۙ‏(30)\nINNAHU MEN SOLAYMAANA WA INNAHU BISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM.\nVerily, it is from Solomon; And it is: “In the name of God the Beneficent, the Most Merciful\nاَلَّا تَعْلُوْا عَلَىَّ وَاْتُوْنِىْ مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nALLAA TA’LOO A’LAYYA WAATOONEE MUSLEMEEN.\nThat “exalt not yourselves against me, and come ye unto me submitting (yourselves to God)\nقَالَتْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَؤُا اَفْتُوْنِىْ فِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ‌ۚ مَا كُنْتُ قَاطِعَةً اَمْرًا حَتّٰى تَشْهَدُوْنِ‏(32)\nQAALAT YAA AYYOHAL MALAO AFTOONEE FEE AMREE, MAA KUNTO QAATE-A’TAN AMRAN HATTAA TASH-HADOON\nSaid she: “O’ ye chiefs! advise me in (this) my affair; (ye know) that I decide not any affair but in your view\nقَالُوْا نَحْنُ اُولُوْا قُوَّةٍ وَّاُولُوْا بَاْسٍ شَدِيْدٍ ۙ وَّالْاَمْرُ اِلَيْكِ فَانْظُرِىْ مَاذَا تَاْمُرِيْنَ‏(33)\nQAALOO NAHNO OOLOO QUWWATIWN WA OOLOO BAA-SIN SHADEED, WAL AMRO ELAYKA FANZUR MAA ZAA TAAMOREEN.\nThey said: “We are endued with strength and possess mighty prowess, and to command is thine: so think (well before) what thou wilt command\nقَالَتْ اِنَّ الْمُلُوْكَ اِذَا دَخَلُوْا قَرْيَةً اَفْسَدُوْهَا وَجَعَلُوْۤا اَعِزَّةَ اَهْلِهَاۤ اَذِلَّةً  ‌ۚ وَكَذٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(34)\nQAALAT INNAL MOLOOKA IZAA DAKHALOO QARYATAN AFSADOOHAA WA JA-A’LOO A-I’ZZATA AHLEHAA AZILLATAH, WA KAZAALEKA YAF-A’LOON.\nSaid (the Queen): “Verily kings, when they enter a town (victorious), ruin it and make the noblest of its people the meanest; and thus will they (also) do.\nوَاِنِّىْ مُرْسِلَةٌ اِلَيْهِمْ بِهَدِيَّةٍ فَنٰظِرَةٌۢ بِمَ يَرْجِعُ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(35)\nWA INNEE MURSELATUN ELAYHIM BEHADIYYATIN FANAAZERATUM BEMA YARJE-O’L MURSALOON.\nAnd verily I will send unto him a present, and (wait to) see with what (answer) return the messengers\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ سُلَيْمٰنَ قَالَ اَتُمِدُّوْنَنِ بِمَالٍ فَمَاۤ اٰتٰٮنِۦَ اللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّاۤ اٰتٰٮكُمْ‌ۚ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ بِهَدِيَّتِكُمْ تَفْرَحُوْنَ‏(36)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A SULAYMAANA QAALA ATOMIDDOONANE BEMAALIN, FAMAA AATAANEYAL LAAHO KHAYRUM MIMMAA AATAAKUM, BAL ANTUM BEHADIYYATEKUM TAFRAHOON.\nAnd when came (the messenger of the Queen) unto Solomon, said (Solomon): “Aid ye me with riches? But what God hath given unto me is better than what He hath given unto you, Aye! it is ye, of your present, exultant.\nاِرْجِعْ اِلَيْهِمْ فَلَنَاْتِيَنَّهُمْ بِجُنُوْدٍ لَّا قِبَلَ لَهُمْ بِهَا وَلَنُخْرِجَنَّهُمْ مِّنْهَاۤ اَذِلَّةً وَّهُمْ صٰغِرُوْنَ‏(37)\nIRJE’ ELAYHIM FALANAATEYANNAHUM BEJONOODIL LAA QEBALA LAHUM BEHAA WA LANUKHREJANNAHUM MINHAA AZILLATAWAN WA HUM SAAGHEROON.\nReturn thou unto them: for we will surely come unto them with (such) hosts which they shall not be able to meet, and certainly will we expel them out therefrom abased, while they shall be contemptible.\nقَالَ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَؤُا اَيُّكُمْ يَاْتِيْنِىْ بِعَرْشِهَا قَبْلَ اَنْ يَّاْتُوْنِىْ مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(38)\nQAALA YAA-AYYOHAL MALA-O AYYOKUM YAATEENEE BE-A’RSHEHAA QABLA AYN YAATOONEE MUSLEMEEN.\nSaid (Solomon): “O’ ye chiefs! which of you can bring unto me her throne, ere they come unto me submitting?\nقَالَ عِفْرِيْتٌ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ اَنَا اٰتِيْكَ بِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ تَقُوْمَ مِنْ مَّقَامِكَ‌ۚ وَاِنِّىْ عَلَيْهِ لَقَوِىٌّ اَمِيْنٌ‏(39)\nQAALA I’FREETUM MENAL JINNE ANAA AATEEKA BEHI QABLA AN TAQOOMA MIM MAQAAMEK, WA INNEE A’LAYHE LAQAWIYYUN AMEEN.\nSaid an audacious one among the jinn; “I will bring it unto thee ere thou risest up from thy place; for verily I am strong (enough to do it) and I am (also thy) trusted one\nقَالَ الَّذِىْ عِنْدَهٗ عِلْمٌ مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ اَنَا اٰتِيْكَ بِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ يَّرْتَدَّ اِلَيْكَ طَرْفُكَ‌ؕ فَلَمَّا رَاٰهُ مُسْتَقِرًّا عِنْدَهٗ قَالَ هٰذَا مِنْ فَضْلِ رَبِّىْ‌ۖ لِيَبْلُوَنِىْٓ ءَاَشْكُرُ اَمْ اَكْفُرُ‌ؕ وَمَنْ شَكَرَ فَاِنَّمَا يَشْكُرُ لِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاِنَّ رَبِّىْ غَنِىٌّ كَرِيْمٌ‏(40)\nQAALAL LAZEE I’NDAHU I’LMUM MENAL KETAABE ANAA AATEEKA BEHI QABLA AYN YARTADDA ELAYKA TARFOK, FALAMMAA RA-AAHO MUSTAQIRRAN I’NDAHU QAALAA HAAZAA MIN FAZLE RABBEE, LEYABLOWANEE, A-ASHKORO AM AKFOR, WA MAN SHAKARA FA-INNAMAA YASHKORO LENAFSEHI, WA MAN KAFARA FA-INNA RABBEE GHANIYYUN KAREEM.\nSaid he with whom was some knowledge (of a part) of the Book: “I will bring it unto thee ere thy eye twinkleth,” and when saw (Solomon) the throne settled besides him, he said: “This is by the grace of my Lord that He may try me if I am grateful or am ungrateful; and he who is grateful, verily he is grateful for his own self, and whoever is ungrateful, then verily my Lord is Self-Sufficient, Bounteous.\nقَالَ نَكِّرُوْا لَهَا عَرْشَهَا نَنْظُرْ اَتَهْتَدِىْۤ اَمْ تَكُوْنُ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(41)\nQAALA NAKKEROO LAHAA A’RSHAHAA NANZOR ATAHTADEE AM TAKOONO MENAL LAZEENA LAA YAHTADOON.\nSaid (Solomon): “Transform her throne for her; we will see if she followeth the way aright, or (she is) of those who go not aright?\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ قِيْلَ اَهٰكَذَا عَرْشُكِ‌ؕ قَالَتْ كَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ‌ۚ وَاُوْتِيْنَا الْعِلْمَ مِنْ قَبْلِهَا وَ كُنَّا مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(42)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AT QEELA A-HAAKAZAA A’RSHOK, QAALAT KA-ANNAHU HOO, WA OOTEENAL I’LMA MIN QABLEHAA WA KUNNAA MUSLEMEEN.\nSo when came (the queen), it was said (unto her): “Is thy throne (also) like this?” Said she: “as it were the same, and we were (already) given the knowledge (of thy apostleship) before it, and we were submitting.\nوَصَدَّهَا مَا كَانَتْ تَّعْبُدُ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّهَا كَانَتْ مِنْ قَوْمٍ كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(43)\nWA SADDAHAA MAA KAANAT TA’BODO MIN DOONIL LAAH, INNAHAA QAANAT MIN QAWMIN KAAFEREEN.\nBut prevented her what she worshipped besides God, verily she was of the disbelieving people.\nقِيْلَ لَهَا ادْخُلِى الصَّرْحَ‌ ۚ فَلَمَّا رَاَتْهُ حَسِبَتْهُ لُجَّةً وَّكَشَفَتْ عَنْ سَاقَيْهَا ‌ؕ قَالَ اِنَّهٗ صَرْحٌ مُّمَرَّدٌ مِّنْ قَوَارِيْرَ ۙ‌قَالَتْ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِىْ وَ اَسْلَمْتُ مَعَ سُلَيْمٰنَ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(44)\nQEELA LAHAD KHOLIS SARH, FALAMMAA RA-ATHO HASEBATHO LUJJATAWN WA KASHAFAT A’N SAAQAYHAA, QAALA INNAHU SARHUM MOMARRADUM MIN QAWAAREER, QAALAT RABBE INNEE ZALAMTO NAFSEE WA ASLAMTO MA-A’ SOLAYMAANA LILLAAHE RABBIL A-A’LAMEEN.\nIt was said unto her: “Enter thou the palace”, but when she saw it she deemed it to be a pool of water and bared her legs; (Solomon) said: “Verily this is but a place smoothed with (slabs of) glass;” said (the Queen): “My Lord! verily I have been unjust to myself, and I submit (along) with Solomon unto God, the Lord of the worlds.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلٰى ثَمُوْدَ اَخَاهُمْ صٰلِحًا اَنِ اعْبُدُوْا اللّٰهَ فَاِذَا هُمْ فَرِيْقٰنِ يَخْتَصِمُوْنَ‏(45)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ELAA SAMOODA AKHAAHUM SAALEHAN ANE’BODUL LAALA FA-IZAA HUM FAREEQAANE YAKHTASEMOON.\nAnd indeed sent We unto (the tribe of) Thamud their brother Salih, saying: “Worship ye God (alone)!” but lo! they became two parties, wrangling (with each other).\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لِمَ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ قَبْلَ الْحَسَنَةِ‌‌ۚ لَوْلَا تَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ اللّٰهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(46)\nQAALA YAA QAWME LEMA TAS-TA’JELOONA BIS-SAYYEATE QABLAL HASANATE, LAWLAA TASTAGHFEROONAL LAAHA LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nSaid (Salih): O’ my people! Why seek ye to hasten on the evil ere the good? Why seek ye not pardon of God? that ye may be shewn mercy.\nقَالُوا اطَّيَّرْنَا بِكَ وَبِمَنْ مَّعَكَ‌ ؕ قَالَ طٰٓئِرُكُمْ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ‌ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(47)\nQAALUT TAYYARNAA BEKA WA BEMAM MA-A’K, QAALA TAAA-EROKUM I’NDAL LAAHE BAL ANTUM QAWMUN TUFTANOON.\nSaid they: “We augur ill from thee and those with thee.” Said (Salih): “Your ill augury is with God; Nay! ye are a people who are being tried.\nوَكَانَ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ تِسْعَةُ رَهْطٍ يُّفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا يُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA KAANA FIL MADEENATE TIS-A’TO RAHTIYN YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE WA LAA YUSLEHOON.\nAnd there were in the town nine men who made mischief in the land and they would not amend (themselves)\nقَالُوْا تَقَاسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ لَنُبَيِّتَنَّهٗ وَ اَهْلَهٗ ثُمَّ لَنَقُوْلَنَّ لِوَلِيِّهٖ مَا شَهِدْنَا مَهْلِكَ اَهْلِهٖ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(49)\nQAALOO TAQAASAMOO BILLAAHE LANOFAYYETANNAHU WA AHLAHU SUMMA LANAQOOLANNA LEWALIYYEHI MAA SHAHIDNAA MAHLEKA AHLEHI WA INNAA LASAADEQOON.\nThey said: “Swear ye to one another by God that surely we will suddenly attack by night, him and his family, and then surely we would say unto his heir we witnessed not the murder of his family, and verily we are truthful.\nوَمَكَرُوْا مَكْرًا وَّمَكَرْنَا مَكْرًا وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA MAKAROO MAKRAWN WA MAKARNAA MAKRAWN WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON\nAnd plotted they and We (too) plotted a plot, and they perceived not.\nفَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ مَكْرِهِمْۙ اَنَّا دَمَّرْنٰهُمْ وَقَوْمَهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(51)\nFANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATO MAKREHIM, ANNAA DAMMARNAAHUM WA QAWMAHUM AJMA-E’EN.\nSee then what was the end of their plot, that We, destroyed them and their people as a whole.\nفَتِلْكَ بُيُوْتُهُمْ خَاوِيَةً ۢ بِمَا ظَلَمُوْا‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(52)\nFATILKA BOYOOTOHUM KHAAWEYATAM BEMAA ZALAMOO, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LEQAWMIYN YA’LAMOON.\nSo those are their houses in empty ruins for they were unjust; Verily there is in this a sign for people who understand.\nوَاَنْجَيْنَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَكَانُوْا يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(53)\nWA ANJAYNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA KAANOO YATTAQOON.\nAnd delivered We those who believed and guarded (themselves) against evil.\nوَلُوْطًا اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَتَاْتُوْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ وَاَنْتُمْ تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(54)\nWA LOOTAN IZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI ATAATOONAL FAAHESHATA WA ANTUM TUBSERAOON.\nAnd (sent We) Lut, when said he unto his people “What! Commit ye filthiness while ye see.\nاَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الرِّجَالَ شَهْوَةً مِّنْ دُوْنِ النِّسَآءِ‌ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(55)\nA-INNAKUM LATAATOO NAR REJAALA SHAHWATAM MIN DOONIN NESAAA, BAL ANTUM QAWMUN TAJHALOON.\nWhat! come ye unto men with lust rather than (unto) women? Verily ye are ignorant people?\nفَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اَخْرِجُوْۤا اٰلَ لُوْطٍ مِّنْ قَرْيَتِكُمْ‌ۚ اِنَّهُمْ اُنَاسٌ يَّتَطَهَّرُوْنَ‏(56)\nFAMAA KAANA JAWAABA QAWMEHI ILLAA AN QAALOO AKHREJOO AALA LOOTIM MIN QARYATEKUM, INNAHUM ONAASUYN YATATAHHAROON.\nBut the answer of his people was naught save that said they: “Turn ye the people of Lut out of your town; Verily they are people (who seek to be) Pure.\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَ اَهْلَهٗۤ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ قَدَّرْنٰهَا مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(57)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WA AHLAHU ILLAM RA-ATAHU, QADDARNAAHAA MENAL GHAABEREEN.\nSo We delivered him and his followers, except his wife; We had decreed her to be of those who remained behind.\nوَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّطَرًا‌ۚ فَسَآءَ مَطَرُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(58)\n58: WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHIM MATARAA, FA-SAAA-A MATARUL MUNZEREEN.\nAnd showered We on them a shower, and evil was the shower of those who had been warned.\nقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى عِبَادِهِ الَّذِيْنَ اصْطَفٰىؕ ءٰۤللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ اَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَؕ‏(59)\nQOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHE WA SALAAMUN A’LAA E’BAADEHIL LAZEENAS TAFAA, AALLAAHO KHAYRUN AMMAA YUSHREKOON.\nSay: “All praise be (only) to God, and peace be on His servants whom He hath chosen: What! Is God better, or what they join (within?)\nاَمَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَاَنْزَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً‌ ۚ فَاَنْۢبَتْنَا بِهٖ حَدَآئِقَ ذَاتَ بَهْجَةٍ‌ ۚ مَا كَانَ لَكُمْ اَنْ تُنْۢبِتُوْا شَجَرَهَا ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ يَّعْدِلُوْنَ ؕ‏(60)\nAMMAN KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA ANZALA LAKUM MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-A, FA-AMBATNAA BEHI HADAAA-EQA ZAATA BAHJAH, MAA KAANA LAKUM AN TUMBETOO SHAJARAHAA, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, BAL HUM QAUMUYN YA’DELOON.\nIs not He Who created the heavens and the earth, and sent down for you water from heaven; then caused We to grow by it gardens beautiful; it was not in your power that ye grow the trees thereof; What! Is there any god with God? Nay! they are a people who (yet) find equals (unto Him)?\nاَمَّنْ جَعَلَ الْاَرْضَ قَرَارًا وَّجَعَلَ خِلٰلَهَاۤ اَنْهٰرًا وَّجَعَلَ لَهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ حَاجِزًا‌ ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ ؕ‏(61)\nAMMAN JA-A’LAL ARZA QARAARAWN WA JA-A’LA KHELAALAHAA ANHAARAWN WA JA-A’LA LAHAA RAWAASEYA WA JA-A’LA BAYNAL BAHRAYNE HAAJEZAA, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nIs not He Who made the earth a resting place, and made in it rivers, and made on it mountains, and caused between two seas a barrier; Is there any god with God? Nay! most of them know not.\nاَمَّنْ يُّجِيْبُ الْمُضْطَرَّ اِذَا دَعَاهُ وَيَكْشِفُ السُّوْٓءَ وَيَجْعَلُكُمْ خُلَفَآءَ الْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ ‌ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ ؕ‏(62)\nAMMAYN YOJEEBUL MUZTARRA EZAA DA-A’AHO WA YAKSHEFUS SOOO-A WA YAJ-A’LOKUM KHOLAFAAA-AL ARZ, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, QALEELAM MAA TAZAKKAROON.\nIs not He Who answereth the distressed one when he calleth Him, and removeth the distress and maketh you the successors in the earth; Is there any god with God? (Nay!) Little it is what ye reflect.\nاَمَّنْ يَّهْدِيْكُمْ فِىْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْبَرِّ وَ الْبَحْرِ وَمَنْ يُّرْسِلُ الرِّيٰحَ بُشْرًۢا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَحْمَتِهٖؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ تَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَؕ‏(63)\nAMMAYN YAHDEEKUM FEE ZOLOMAATIL BARRE WAL BAHRE WA MAYN YURSELUR REYAAHA BUSHRAM BAYNA YADAY RAHMATEH, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, TA-A’ALAL LAAHO A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nIs not He Who guideth you in the darkness of the land and the sea, and Who sendeth the winds as the bearers of the good news of His Mercy? Is there any god with God? Exalted High is God above what they associate (with Him).\nاَمَّنْ يَّبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ وَمَنْ يَّرْزُقُكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ ءَاِلٰهٌ مَّعَ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(64)\nAMMAYN YABDAUL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOHU WA MAYN YARZOQOKUM MENAS SAMAAA-E WAL-ARZ, A-ELAAHUM MA-A’L LAAH, QUL HAATOO BURHAANAKUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nIs not He Who originateth the creation, then reproduceth it, and Who provideth for you sustenance from the heaven and the earth? Is there any god with God? Say: “Bring ye your proof, if ye be truthful.\nقُلْ لَّا يَعْلَمُ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ الْغَيْبَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ‌ؕ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(65)\nQUL LAA YA’LAMO MAN FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZIL GHAYBA ILLAL LAAH, WA MAA YASHO’ROONA AYYAANA YUB-A’SOON.\nSay: “None (either) in the heavens or in the earth knoweth the unseen save God; And they perceive not when they shall be raised\nبَلِ ادّٰرَكَ عِلْمُهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ‌ بَلْ هُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهَا  بَلْ هُمْ مِّنْهَا عَمُوْنَ‏(66)\nBALID DAARAKA I’LMOHUM FIL AAKHERAH, BAL HUM FEE SHAKKIM MINHAA, BAL HUM MINHAA A’MOON.\nNay! hath reached them the knowledge about the hereafter; Nay! they are in doubt about it; Nay! they are blind unto it.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا تُرٰبًا وَّاٰبَآؤُنَاۤ اَئِنَّا لَمُخْرَجُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO A-EZAA KUNNAA TORAABAWN WA AABAAA-ONAA A-INNAA LAMUKHRAJOON.\nAnd say those who disbelieve: “What! when we have become dust, and our fathers (too), shall we certainly be brought forth (again)?\nلَقَدْ وُعِدْنَا هٰذَا نَحْنُ وَاٰبَآؤُنَا مِنْ قَبْلُۙ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(68)\nLAQAD WO-I’DNAA HAAZAA NAHNO WA AABAAA-ONAA MIN QABLO, IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nIndeed we had been promised this, we and our fathers before (too); (But) these are naught but stories of yore\nقُلْ سِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(69)\nQUL SEEROO FIL ARZE FANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUJREMEEN.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Travel ye in the earth and see how was the end of the guilty (ones)\nوَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا تَكُنْ فِىْ ضَيْقٍ مِّمَّا يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(70)\nWA LAA TAHZAN A’LAYHIM WA LAA TAKUN FEE ZAYQIM MIMMAA YAMKOROON.\nAnd grieve thou not for them and be not distressed of what they devise.\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(71)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAL WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd say they: “When shall this promise (of chastisement) come to pass, if ye be truthful?\nقُلْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ رَدِفَ لَكُمْ بَعْضُ الَّذِىْ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(72)\nQUL A’SAA AYN YAKOONA RADEFA LAKUM BA’ZUL LAZEE TASTA’JELOON.\nSay thou: “Maybe that it is after you, a part of what ye seek to hasten.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(73)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAZOO FAZLIN A’LAN NAASE WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YASHKOROON.\nAnd verily thy Lord is the Lord of grace unto the people but most of them thank not.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُكِنُّ صُدُوْرُهُمْ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(74)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LA-YA’LAMO MAA TOKINNO SODOOROHUM WA MAA YO’LENOON.\nAnd verily thy Lord well-knoweth what do enshroud their breasts and what they declare.\nوَمَا مِنْ غَآئِبَةٍ فِى السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(75)\nWA MAA MIN GHAAA-EBATIN FIS SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nNothing is there hidden in the heavens and the earth but it is in the manifest Book.\nاِنَّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ يَقُصُّ عَلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اَكْثَرَ الَّذِىْ هُمْ فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(76)\nINNA HAAZAL QURAANA YAQUSSO A’LAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA AKSARAL LAZEE HUM FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nVerily this Qur’an relateth unto the children of Israel most of what they therein disagree.\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(77)\nWA INNAHU LAHODAWN WA RAHMATUL LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nAnd verily it is a (sure) guidance and mercy unto the believers.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِىْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِحُكْمِهٖ‌ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْعَلِيْمُ ۙ‌ۚ‏(78)\nINNA RABBAKA YAQZEE BAYNAHUM BEHUKMEH, WA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL A’LEEM.\nVerily, thy Lord will judge between them by His (Own) decree, and He is the All- Mighty, All-Knowing.\nفَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّكَ عَلَى الْحَقِّ الْمُبِيْنِ‏(79)\nFATAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAH, INNAKA A’LAL HAQQIL MOBEEN.\nThen rely thou on God; verily thou art on the manifest truth.\nاِنَّكَ لَا تُسْمِعُ الْمَوْتٰى وَلَا تُسْمِعُ الصُّمَّ الدُّعَآءَ اِذَا وَلَّوْا مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(80)\nINNAKA LAA TUSME-U’L MAWTAA WA LAA TUSME-U’S SUMMAD DO-A’AA-A EZAA WALLAW MUDBEREEN.\nVerily thou canst not make the dead to listen nor canst thou make the deaf to hear the call when they turn away backward.\nوَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِهٰدِى الْعُمْىِ عَنْ ضَلٰلَتِهِمْ‌ؕ اِنْ تُسْمِعُ اِلَّا مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَهُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(81)\nWA MAA ANTA BEHAADIL U’MYE A’N ZALAALATEHIM, IN TUSME-O’ ILLAA MAYN YOAMENO BE-AAYAATENAA FAHUM MUSLEMOON.\nAnd nor canst thou be a guide unto the Blind against their straying; thou canst make none hear save those who believe in Our signs, so they have submitted themselves.\nوَ اِذَا وَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ اَخْرَجْنَا لَهُمْ دَآبَّةً مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ تُكَلِّمُهُمْۙ اَنَّ النَّاسَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا لَا يُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(82)\nWA EZAA WAQA-A’L QAWLO A’LAYHIM AKHRAJNAA LAHUM DAAAB-BATAM MENAL ARZE TOKALLEMOHUM, ANNAN NAASA KAANOO BE-AAYAATENAA LAA YOOQENOON.\nAnd when the word shall come to pass on them, We shall bring forth unto them, a walking one from the earth who shall speak unto them, that the people believed not (with certainty') in Our signs.\nوَ يَوْمَ نَحْشُرُ مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ فَوْجًا مِّمَّنْ يُّكَذِّبُ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَهُمْ يُوْزَعُوْنَ‏(83)\nWA YAWMA NAHSHORO MIN KULLE UMMATIN FAWJAM MIMMAYN YOKAZZEBO BE-AAYAATENAA FAHUM YOOZA-O’ON.\nAnd on the day when We will collect from every people a party from those who belied our signs, then will they be formed into groups.\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءُوْ قَالَ اَكَذَّبْتُمْ بِاٰيٰتِىْ وَلَمْ تُحِيْطُوْا بِهَا عِلْمًا اَمَّاذَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(84)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-OO QAALA AKAZZABTUM BE-AAYAATEE WA LAM TOHEETOO BEHAA I’LMAA AMMAA ZAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nTill they come before God (who will) say “Belied ye My signs while ye comprehended them not in your knowledge? or what is it ye were doing?\nوَوَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِمَا ظَلَمُوْا فَهُمْ لَا يَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA WAQA-A’L QAWLO A’LAYHIM BEMAA ZALAMOO FAHUM LAA YANTEQOON.\nAnd the word shall come to pass on them for they were unjust, and they shall speak not.\nاَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا جَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ لِيَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(86)\nALAM YARAW ANNAA JA-A’LNAL LAYLA LEYASKONOO FEEHE WAN NAHAARA MUBSERAA, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMIYN YOAMENOON.\nWhat! See they not that We have made the night that they may rest therein, and the day with light (to see); Verily, in this are signs for the people who believe?\nوَيَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِىْ الصُّوْرِ فَفَزِعَ مَنْ فِىْ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا مَنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ‌ؕ وَكُلٌّ اَتَوْهُ دٰخِرِيْنَ‏(87)\nWA YAWMA YUNFAKHO FIS SOORE FA-FAZE-A’ MAN FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZE ILLAAMAN SHAAA-AL LAAH, WA KULLUN ATAWHO DAAKHEREEN.\nAnd the day when there shall be blown the Trumpet, and those in the heavens and those in the earth shall be terrorized, save him whom God willeth, and all shall come unto Him abased.\nوَتَرَى الْجِبَالَ تَحْسَبُهَا جَامِدَةً وَّهِىَ تَمُرُّ مَرَّ السَّحَابِ‌ؕ صُنْعَ اللّٰهِ الَّذِىْۤ اَتْقَنَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(88)\nWA TARAL JEBAALA TAHSABOHAA JAAMEDATAWN WA HEYA TAMURRO MARRAS SAHAAB, SUN-A’L LAAHIL LAZEE ATQANA KULLA SHAY-IN, INNAHU KHABEERUM BEMAA TAF-A’LOON.\nAnd thou wilt see the mountains which thinkest thou firm, solid, pass away the pas sing of the clouds. It is the work of God Who hath made everything firm; Verily He is All-Aware of what (all) ye do.\nمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهٗ خَيْرٌ مِّنْهَا‌ۚ وَهُمْ مِّنْ فَزَعٍ يَّوْمَئِذٍ اٰمِنُوْنَ‏(89)\nMAN JAAA-A BIL-HASANATE FALAHU KHARUM MINHAA, WA HUM MIN FAZA-I’YN YAWMA-EZIN AAMENOON.\nWhosoever bringeth good, for him shall be better than it and they, of the terror of the day, be secure.\nوَمَنْ جَآءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَكُبَّتْ وُجُوْهُهُمْ فِى النَّارِؕ هَلْ تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(90)\nWA MAN JAAA-A BIS-SAYYE-ATE FAKUBBAT WOJOOHOHUM FIN NAAR, HAL TUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd whosoever bringeth evil, these shall be cast down on their faces, in the (Hell) fire; Ye shall be recompensed for aught save what ye were doing.\nاِنَّمَاۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ رَبَّ هٰذِهِ الْبَلْدَةِ الَّذِىْ حَرَّمَهَا وَلَهٗ كُلُّ شَىْءٍ‌ وَّاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَۙ‏(91)\nINNAMAA UMIRTO AN A-A’BODA RABBA HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEE HARRAMAHAA WA LAHU KULLO SHAYIWN, WA UMIRTO AN A-A’BODA RABBA HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEE HARRAMAHAA WA LAHU KULLO SHAY-IWN, WA UMIRTO AN AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\n(Say thou unto them O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I commanded only that I should serve the Lord of this city, Who am hath made it sacred, and His are all things, and commanded I am that I should be of the Muslims (those who have submitted themselves to God),\nوَاَنْ اَتْلُوَا الْقُرْاٰنَ‌ۚ فَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِىْ لِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُنْذِرِيْنَ‏(92)\nWA AN ATLOWAL QURAAN, FAMANEH TADAA FA-INNAMAA YAHTADEE LENAFSEH, WA MAN ZALLA FAQUL INNAMAA ANAA MENAL MUNZEREEN.\nAnd that I should recite the Qur’an: so whosoever is guided aright, he is guided aright for his (own self), and whosoever goeth astray, then say thou: “I am only of the warners.\nوَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ سَيُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ فَتَعْرِفُوْنَهَا‌ ؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHE SAYOREEKUM AAYAATEHI FA-TA’REFOONAHAA, WA MAA RABBOKA BEGHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nAnd say thou, “All praise is God’s. Soon will He show you His signs that ye shall recognise them;” and thy Lord is not heed less of what all ye do.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Naml (The Ant)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 93 verses. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan, it is written that the reward for reciting this Surah is compared to ten times the number of people alive during the time of Prophets Sulaiman (a.s.), Hud (a.s.), Shoa’ib (a.s.), Saaleh (a.s.) and Ibrahim (a.s.).\nIn the commentary of Burhan it is written that if this Surah is written on deerskin and kept in the house, then no dangerous creature (e.g. snake) will come near the house. This has been narrated by Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.)."
